{
  "mark.4.p1.b1": {
    "text": "Once again Jesus began to teach beside the sea,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p1.b2": {
    "text": "And such a large crowd gathered around Him",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p1.b3": {
    "text": "That He got into a boat and sat in it,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p1.b4": {
    "text": "While all the people crowded along the shore.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p1.b5": {
    "text": "And He taught them many things in parables,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p1.b6": {
    "text": "And in His teaching He said,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p2.b1": {
    "text": "Listen!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p2.b2": {
    "text": "A farmer went out to sow his seed.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p2.b3": {
    "text": "And as he was sowing, some seed fell along the path,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p2.b4": {
    "text": "And the birds came and devoured it.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p3.b1": {
    "text": "Some fell on rocky ground, where it did not have much soil.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p3.b2": {
    "text": "It sprang up quickly because the soil was shallow.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p3.b3": {
    "text": "But when the sun rose, the seedlings were scorched, and they withered because they had no root.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p3.b4": {
    "text": "Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p3.b5": {
    "text": "And choked the seedlings, and they yielded no crop.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p4.b1": {
    "text": "Still other seed fell on good soil, where it sprouted, grew up, and produced a crop—",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p4.b2": {
    "text": "One bearing thirtyfold,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p4.b3": {
    "text": "Another sixtyfold,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p4.b4": {
    "text": "And another a hundredfold.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p4.b5": {
    "text": "Then Jesus said,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p4.b6": {
    "text": "He who has ears to hear, let him hear.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b1": {
    "text": "As soon as Jesus was alone with the Twelve and those around Him,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b2": {
    "text": "They asked Him about the parable.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b3": {
    "text": "He replied,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b4": {
    "text": "The mystery of the kingdom of God has been given to you,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b5": {
    "text": "But to those on the outside everything is expressed in parables,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b6": {
    "text": "So that, they may be ever seeing but never perceiving,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b7": {
    "text": "And ever hearing but never understanding;",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p5.b8": {
    "text": "Otherwise they might turn and be forgiven.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p6.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus said to them,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p6.b2": {
    "text": "Do you not understand this parable?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p6.b3": {
    "text": "Then how will you understand any of the parables?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p6.b4": {
    "text": "The farmer sows the word.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p6.b5": {
    "text": "Some are like the seeds along the path, where the word is sown. As soon as they hear it,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p6.b6": {
    "text": "Satan comes and takes away the word that was sown in them.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p7.b1": {
    "text": "Some are like the seeds sown on rocky ground. They hear the word",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p7.b2": {
    "text": "And at once receive it with joy.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p7.b3": {
    "text": "But they themselves have no root, and they remain for only a season.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p7.b4": {
    "text": "When trouble or persecution comes because of the word,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p7.b5": {
    "text": "They quickly fall away.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p8.b1": {
    "text": "Others are like the seeds sown among the thorns. They hear the word,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p8.b2": {
    "text": "But the worries of this life, the deceitfulness of wealth, and the desire for other things come in",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p8.b3": {
    "text": "And choke the word, and it becomes unfruitful.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p8.b4": {
    "text": "Still others are like the seeds sown on good soil. They hear the word, receive it, and produce a crop—",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p8.b5": {
    "text": "Thirtyfold, sixtyfold, or a hundredfold.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b1": {
    "text": "Jesus also said to them,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b2": {
    "text": "Does anyone bring in a lamp",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b3": {
    "text": "To put it under a basket",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b4": {
    "text": "Or under a bed?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b5": {
    "text": "Doesn’t he set it on a stand?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b6": {
    "text": "For there is nothing hidden that will not be disclosed,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b7": {
    "text": "And nothing concealed that will not be brought to light.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p9.b8": {
    "text": "If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p10.b1": {
    "text": "He went on to say,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p10.b2": {
    "text": "Pay attention to what you hear.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p10.b3": {
    "text": "With the measure you use,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p10.b4": {
    "text": "It will be measured to you,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p10.b5": {
    "text": "And even more will be added to you.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p10.b6": {
    "text": "For whoever has will be given more.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:25"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p10.b7": {
    "text": "But whoever does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:25"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b1": {
    "text": "Jesus also said,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b2": {
    "text": "The kingdom of God is like a man who scatters seed on the ground.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b3": {
    "text": "Night and day he sleeps",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b4": {
    "text": "And wakes,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b5": {
    "text": "And the seed sprouts and grows,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b6": {
    "text": "Though he knows not how.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b7": {
    "text": "All by itself the earth produces a crop—",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b8": {
    "text": "First the stalk, then the head, then grain that ripens within.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b9": {
    "text": "And as soon as the grain is ripe, he swings the sickle,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p11.b10": {
    "text": "Because the harvest has come.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p12.b1": {
    "text": "Then He asked,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p12.b2": {
    "text": "To what can we compare the kingdom of God?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p12.b3": {
    "text": "With what parable shall we present it?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p12.b4": {
    "text": "It is like a mustard seed,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p12.b5": {
    "text": "Which is the smallest of all seeds sown upon the earth.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p12.b6": {
    "text": "But after it is planted, it grows to be the largest of all garden plants",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p12.b7": {
    "text": "And puts forth great branches, so that the birds of the air nest in its shade.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p13.b1": {
    "text": "With many such parables Jesus spoke the word to them, to the extent that they could understand.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p13.b2": {
    "text": "He did not tell them anything without using a parable.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p13.b3": {
    "text": "But privately He explained everything to His own disciples.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p13.b4": {
    "text": "When that evening came, He said to His disciples,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:35"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p13.b5": {
    "text": "Let us cross to the other side.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:35"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p14.b1": {
    "text": "After they had dismissed the crowd,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:36"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p14.b2": {
    "text": "They took Jesus with them, since He was already in the boat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:36"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p14.b3": {
    "text": "And there were other boats with Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:36"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p14.b4": {
    "text": "Soon a violent windstorm came up,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:37"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p14.b5": {
    "text": "And the waves were breaking over the boat, so that it was being swamped.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:37"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p15.b1": {
    "text": "But Jesus was in the stern, sleeping on the cushion.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p15.b2": {
    "text": "So they woke Him and said,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p15.b3": {
    "text": "Teacher,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p15.b4": {
    "text": "Don’t You care that we are perishing?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p16.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus got up",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:39"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p16.b2": {
    "text": "And rebuked the wind and the sea. … He commanded.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:39"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p16.b3": {
    "text": "Silence! … Be still!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:39"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p16.b4": {
    "text": "And the wind died down, and it was perfectly calm.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:39"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p17.b1": {
    "text": "He asked.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:40"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p17.b2": {
    "text": "Why are you so afraid?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:40"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p17.b3": {
    "text": "Do you still have no faith?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:40"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p17.b4": {
    "text": "Overwhelmed with fear, they asked one another,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:41"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p17.b5": {
    "text": "Who is this,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:41"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.4.p17.b6": {
    "text": "That even the wind and the sea obey Him?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 4:41"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  }
}
